WEBVTT

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:08.900
Go, Hammer-Rush!

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.940
Direct Attack!

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.040
C'mon, stand up! This Duel ain't over yet!

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.710
I beg you! Please forgive me!

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.750
I'll never try to cheat again!

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.540
Stand up, you no good bastard!

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:29.130
That's enough already, Gauche.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:29.710
Huh?

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:33.670
Our true job is to search for Numbers.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:36.550
Looks like Droite's good spirit saved you.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:38.890
Now disappear from Heartland City this instant!

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:41.810
Shitty bastard...

00:00:55.700 --> 00:00:57.320
I overslept!

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.870
That's right, that's right!

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:05.040
It was back during the opening ceremony of the World Duel Carnival.

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:07.960
<i>I'm off!</i>

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:14.920
But after separating from Yuma and the others, I hid here to analyze the other Duelists.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:20.260
And I ended up sleeping through the entire day!

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:24.930
I gotta start collecting Heart Pieces, or I ain't gonna make it into the finals!

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:26.520
Hold on.

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.350
It's already the second day of the tournament.

00:01:28.350 --> 00:01:31.150
More than likely, only a ton of strong guys remain.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:35.940
If I should lose a Duel and lose this thing in the process, it's all over.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:37.650
I wonder what I should do.

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:41.410
I just thought up a good plan!

00:01:48.170 --> 00:01:51.920
I did it! Now I've got four Heart Pieces!

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.460
You just need one more to advance to the finals.

00:01:55.420 --> 00:01:56.800
No biggie!

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:58.180
Huh?

00:01:58.180 --> 00:01:59.430
What's the matter?

00:01:59.430 --> 00:02:01.300
Astral's gone.

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:02.890
Astral is?

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:08.100
Well, at least I get to Duel my way while he isn't around.

00:02:15.320 --> 00:02:17.990
Numbers... My memories...

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.370
Just what in the world am I?

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:33.420
Darn!

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.300
Hey, Taichi! What're you doing?

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:37.760
Yuma! Kotori!

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.260
Have you seen Tokunosuke?

00:02:39.260 --> 00:02:40.720
Tokunosuke?

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:41.970
He's so cruel!

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:46.010
<i>Wow, you're participating in the Duel Carnival, Taichi?</i>

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:48.680
<i>Yup, and you better believe I'm after the championship.</i>

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:52.900
<i>If that's how you feel, I bet you gathered up a considerable amount of Heart Pieces.</i>

00:02:52.900 --> 00:02:56.530
<i>No, not exactly... It's a bit pitiful, actually.</i>

00:02:56.530 --> 00:02:58.190
<i>Oh?</i>

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:02.570
<i>Come this way!</i>

00:03:02.570 --> 00:03:03.990
<i>Wh-What the heck?</i>

00:03:04.320 --> 00:03:06.030
<i>Look here.</i>

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:07.870
<i>You collected that many?</i>

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.960
<i>Let me see your Heart Piece for a minute.</i>

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:11.750
<i>Hey!</i>

00:03:11.750 --> 00:03:14.210
<i>What's the big deal? Give it back!</i>

00:03:19.380 --> 00:03:20.760
<i>It's a match!</i>

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:23.090
<i>I'll be taking this Heart Piece.</i>

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:23.640
<i>Wha?</i>

00:03:23.640 --> 00:03:28.640
<i>In return, you can pick all the Heart Pieces you want from this bag.</i>

00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:30.310
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:32.060
- Huh?!
 - Huh?!

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.020
So you're disqualified?!

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:35.360
Y-Yeah...

00:03:35.360 --> 00:03:38.690
I mean, the Heart Pieces all have a specific pattern carved into their edges.

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.280
Otherwise they won't fit together.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:44.320
But the Heart Pieces he gave me were fake!

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:45.740
They were candy!

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.200
- Candy?!
 - Candy?!

00:03:48.580 --> 00:03:51.460
I thought they were suspicious looking, so I licked them and this happened.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.210
Thanks to that, the edges are all stuck together.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:57.670
This happened because you tried to get Heart Pieces improperly, you know!

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.800
You've got a point, but...

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:02.630
Can you please help me look for Tokunosuke?!

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.180
Guess there's no helping it.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:07.930
What's the deal?!

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:09.680
It melted!

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.430
You're kiddin' me!

00:04:11.890 --> 00:04:13.940
How dare he trick me!

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:15.060
Hold it!

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:15.850
Whoa!

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:18.230
What happened?

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:22.190
All the people in this place are so stupid they don't even realize the law that states there's a flip side to everything.

00:04:22.190 --> 00:04:27.200
Thanks to them, I was able to gather four Heart Pieces without having to Duel even once.

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:28.700
Hmm?

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:32.160
Which means if I choose one of the pieces from inside this bag...

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.960
I can pass right to the finals!

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.590
Darn! Where the heck did that Tokunosuke go?!

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:40.920
I can't believe he's gathering Heart Pieces like this!

00:04:41.590 --> 00:04:43.300
- If he's collected them, then...!
 - If he's collected them, then...!

00:04:53.270 --> 00:04:54.980
I'm done!

00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:56.690
Here he is.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:02.110
I collected all the Heart Pieces!

00:05:02.110 --> 00:05:04.070
Oh, you already collected them?

00:05:04.070 --> 00:05:05.610
Aren't you in high spirits?

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:09.490
Does that mean I'm the first one here?

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:13.160
Yippee! I'm the first one to advance to the finals!

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:15.790
I want you to lick it.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:18.880
Huh? You talking about my Heart Pieces?

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:22.170
B-But Heart Pieces aren't made for licking.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:25.800
A-And they're bound to be dirty after being in people's pockets.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.890
Then should I grab your mouth and <i>make</i> you do it?

00:05:28.890 --> 00:05:31.350
I'll lick it! I just need to lick it, right?

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:39.310
It melted!

00:05:40.770 --> 00:05:42.400
Why did it melt?

00:05:42.400 --> 00:05:45.280
Whoa! This is candy!

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.410
You lying, thieving little cheapskate! Screw you!

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:51.240
Ow, ow, ow...

00:05:54.910 --> 00:05:57.370
What the hell are <i>those</i> supposed to be?!

00:05:57.370 --> 00:06:00.880
I-It wasn't me! I-I was tricked!

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:14.810
Pipe down!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.770
- Leg'go!
 - Tokunosuke!

00:06:18.460 --> 00:06:21.130
<i>As I get closer, I stretch my hand out</i>

00:06:21.130 --> 00:06:24.180
<i>towards that shining light leading towards tomorrow</i>

00:06:24.350 --> 00:06:31.440
<i>I dream of a world that expands from my feet.</i>

00:06:35.190 --> 00:06:40.700
<i>I haven't a clue of where things like dreams and hopes are at.</i>

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:45.200
<i>Even if I run looking for it, I still can't seem to find it.</i>

00:06:46.160 --> 00:06:51.660
<i>I wonder if I have fallen into a gap of truth and lies.</i>

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:56.460
<i>Even so, our grand tale has yet to begin.</i>

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:02.130
<i>Let's move on towards tomorrow, 
even if our road begins to fall apart.</i>

00:07:02.130 --> 00:07:07.390
<i>I will jump forward, before all my
 strength completely drains.</i>

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:10.270
<i>The closer I get, the further it becomes,</i>

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:13.560
<i>that truth that I must seize.</i>

00:07:13.560 --> 00:07:18.730
<i>It's to find hope that we desire from a future unseen.</i>

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:21.320
<i>With a heart stronger than anyone else,</i>

00:07:21.530 --> 00:07:24.490
<i>I'll learn to keep running up.</i>

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:30.040
<i>With the strength to win any battle, 
despite just how weak I am,</i>

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.540
<i>My purpose is to find,</i>

00:07:32.540 --> 00:07:35.540
<i>with these invaluable friends of mine,</i>

00:07:35.540 --> 00:07:42.340
<i>The future of the world expanding
 from my feet with my own eyes.</i>

00:07:48.230 --> 00:07:49.940
I said to pipe down!

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.780
No way! I'm gonna start crying!

00:07:53.410 --> 00:07:54.740
Tokunosuke!

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:56.700
Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:07:56.700 --> 00:08:01.370
"Number 37: Disqualified from the W.D.C.!?
 Heartland's Assassins Droite and Gauche"

00:07:56.700 --> 00:07:59.660
What are you trying to do with Tokunosuke?!

00:07:59.660 --> 00:08:01.870
Who the hell are <i>you</i>?

00:08:02.540 --> 00:08:03.830
You're...

00:08:04.500 --> 00:08:06.840
That noisy little boy from before.

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:10.210
So that was you?

00:08:10.210 --> 00:08:13.180
I asked you what you plan to do with Tokunosuke!

00:08:13.180 --> 00:08:15.930
He fabricated Heart Pieces!

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:17.970
As punishment, his deck will be confiscated!

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:20.890
He'll be disqualified and deprived of all future participation in the Duel Carnival for the rest of his life!

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:25.350
I'll make it so he can never Duel again before beating his ass right out of Heartland City!

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:29.360
H-Hang on a minute! You don't have to go that far!

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.070
"That far"?!

00:08:31.070 --> 00:08:34.240
This pest's dishonored Dueling!

00:08:34.240 --> 00:08:36.030
I cannot forgive him for that!

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:43.080
Spare me! I'll give you my deck or whatever you want!

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.170
Hey, hold it!

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:48.880
It's true that what Tokunosuke did may be unforgivable.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.840
But that's no reason for you to go this far!

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:54.300
If this is an issue between Duelists, let's settle it with a Duel!

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:57.510
If you insist on taking Tokunosuke, Duel with me!

00:08:58.350 --> 00:09:00.060
A Duel, you say?

00:09:00.060 --> 00:09:03.140
Interesting! But I'm strong, you know!

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:04.940
Hmph, that's just fine!

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.650
You can both come at me at the same time!

00:09:06.650 --> 00:09:07.770
Very well.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:09.570
This Duel will be 2-on-1.

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:14.820
If you Duel against the both of us and manage to defeat the both of us, it's your win.

00:09:14.820 --> 00:09:16.780
And we'll forget about what he did.

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:22.500
But if you end up losing, <i>you</i> will be required to take the punishment in his place.

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.000
No way!

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:27.370
How about it? You on board?

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:38.760
Hmph. Don't act like you've got the balls to fight when you're nothing but an incompetent Duelist not even worth talking to.

00:09:38.760 --> 00:09:42.220
All right! I accept that Duel!

00:09:43.430 --> 00:09:44.730
What?

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:47.850
Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:52.570
But if you lose and they take your deck, you won't be able to continue participating in the Carnival.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:59.030
And Astral's still not here, right? It's way to reckless for you to fight both of them by yourself, Yuma!

00:09:59.030 --> 00:10:03.160
Even so, I can't just abandon Tokunosuke, my friend!

00:10:04.250 --> 00:10:08.170
Sounds interesting! I'll test out that spirit of yours!

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:12.380
Here I go! I won't let myself lose to the likes of you!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:15.970
Duel Disk, set!

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.600
D-Gazer, set!

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.850
Duel Disk, set!

00:10:38.610 --> 00:10:40.910
<i>AR Vision - Link established.</i>

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:43.660
Duel!!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:20.700
It's no good. I can't remember anything past that.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:27.490
And there's that miracle that saved Yuma and I during the Duel with Kaito.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.540
What exactly is the "Power of ZeXal"?

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:39.630
Yuma's starting a Duel?

00:11:39.630 --> 00:11:41.090
I have to get going.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:43.260
It's been a long time, Astral!

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:48.310
You're...!

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:50.310
Number 96!

00:11:57.270 --> 00:11:58.690
Why are you...?

00:11:58.690 --> 00:12:00.360
You broke the seal?!

00:12:00.360 --> 00:12:04.110
Yes, it was what we Numbers wanted!

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:05.280
"We"?

00:12:13.580 --> 00:12:16.130
Let's hurry up and finish this, Gauche.

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.290
I know.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:19.800
Astral's not here?!

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:22.050
God, this is so reckless!

00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.890
There's no way Yuma can beat those two on his own!

00:12:24.890 --> 00:12:27.850
Hey! Who do you think he's fighting for?!

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:30.270
Yuma-<i>kun</i>, you can do it!

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:34.230
Heck yeah! I'm good enough to handle these two on my own!

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:35.350
Here goes!

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.480
My turn! Draw!

00:12:38.020 --> 00:12:40.820
I set a Monster in face-down Defense Mode!

00:12:41.610 --> 00:12:44.990
I then set a card face-down and end my turn!

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:49.200
Heh! All that talk and you go and play on the defensive.

00:12:50.120 --> 00:12:53.210
I can't afford to lose this Duel!

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.670
Why are the other Numbers giving you their strength?

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.710
I already told you. It's what all the Numbers <i>want</i>.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:03.630
You want the same! The destruction of the world!

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:04.680
Destruction?

00:13:04.680 --> 00:13:06.090
Impossible!

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:10.100
You're saying I want to destroy the world?!

00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:12.560
If you didn't, how can you explain my being here?!

00:13:14.810 --> 00:13:17.480
My turn! Draw!

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:20.480
I Summon Phantom Butterfly Assassin Morpho!

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:30.160
I then set two cards and end my turn!

00:13:31.120 --> 00:13:33.120
1200 Attack Points...!

00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:37.290
You'll regret the spirit you had to challenge us to a match!

00:13:37.290 --> 00:13:39.840
My turn! Draw!

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:43.210
I Special Summon Hammer-Rush Bouncer!

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:55.060
This card can be Special Summoned from my hand when my field is empty while my opponent controls a Monster, Magic, or Trap Card!

00:13:55.060 --> 00:13:57.440
It's got 2300 Attack Points!

00:13:57.440 --> 00:14:00.310
He Summoned a Level Six Monster right off the bat!

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:02.570
I end my turn with that.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:04.820
Now come at us with everything you've got!

00:14:04.820 --> 00:14:08.740
<i>My opponents have a Monster with 1200 Attack Power and another with 2300 Attack Power.</i>

00:14:09.700 --> 00:14:12.240
<i>And in my hand...</i>

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:15.250
Okay! I decided which of you I'm gonna beat first!

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:17.460
My turn! Draw!

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:21.420
I switch my face-down Defense Mode Monster into face-up Attack Mode!

00:14:22.670 --> 00:14:24.590
Show yourself, Rai Rider!

00:14:26.010 --> 00:14:28.800
Hmph. It's got 1200 Attack Points.

00:14:28.800 --> 00:14:31.430
What can that piss-poor Monster possibly do?

00:14:31.430 --> 00:14:33.220
Hmph! Just you watch!

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.600
I'll then Summon Tasuke Knight!

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:47.440
Yes! If I destroy Morpho with Tasuke Knight and then Direct Attack with Rai Rider, I'll deal her great damage!

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:50.950
Go, Tasuke Knight! Attack Morpho!

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.910
Wave Pressure!

00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:57.370
I activate the Permanent Trap, Scales of Subordination!

00:14:57.370 --> 00:15:00.670
When an opposing Monster declares an attack,

00:15:00.670 --> 00:15:06.840
this card can change this card into an Equipment Card and change the target's Battle Position from Attack to Defense Position!

00:15:06.840 --> 00:15:07.550
What?!

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:15.600
Tasuke Knight's attack was stopped!

00:15:16.520 --> 00:15:20.440
Looks like your spirit leads you to rush in and miscalculate!

00:15:20.440 --> 00:15:22.310
I'll end my turn.

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:25.770
He can't win without Astral around after all!

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:28.650
Why won't Astral come out?!

00:15:29.610 --> 00:15:34.070
C'mon, remember your mission, Astral!

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:39.540
Now! Come to our side, Astral!

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:41.710
Astral!!

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.420
What?!

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:50.130
Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:54.800
Hope, does this mean you've decided to stand against us?

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:59.350
Fine then! I'll just start by absorbing you first!

00:16:01.520 --> 00:16:04.440
Come out, Black Mist!

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:18.450
My turn! Draw!

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:22.040
I Summon Phantom Butterfly Assassin Swallowtail!

00:16:25.790 --> 00:16:30.170
And I activate the second effect of Scales of Subordination!

00:16:30.170 --> 00:16:35.590
Once per turn, I can change the Battle Position of the Monster this card is equipped to.

00:16:35.590 --> 00:16:39.060
I switch Tasuke Knight into Attack Mode!

00:16:39.060 --> 00:16:42.810
So she's gonna attack him with her Phantom Butterfly Assassin?

00:16:42.810 --> 00:16:46.520
But I'll only take 100 points of damage if you do attack him!

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:47.810
Naive.

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:50.730
I activate the Monster Effect of Phantom Butterfly Assassin Morph!

00:16:50.730 --> 00:16:58.410
Once per turn, when an opponent's Monster changes its Battle Position, she can decrease its Attack and Defense Power by 1000 points!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:16:59.200
Oh crap!

00:16:59.200 --> 00:17:01.700
Tasuke Knight's Attack Power!

00:17:01.700 --> 00:17:06.210
I use Phantom Butterfly Assassin Morph to attack Tasuke Knight!

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:08.210
Blue Scale Stream!

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:20.220
I then activate the Monster Effect of Phantom Butterfly Assassin Swallowtail!

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:24.310
When a Monster on the field inflicts Battle Damage other than this card,

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:28.310
one of my opponent's Monsters loses Attack Power equal to that damage.

00:17:29.520 --> 00:17:32.230
Now even Rai Rider's Attack Power was decreased!

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:36.200
I then use Phantom Butterfly Assassin Swallowtail to attack Rai Rider!

00:17:36.200 --> 00:17:38.070
Limit Scale Stream!

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.260
Yuma!

00:17:53.260 --> 00:17:55.260
He's only got 2400 Life Points!

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:58.340
I can't believe he lost 1600 points in one go!

00:17:58.340 --> 00:18:04.100
I thought you had more guts than this, but you turned out to be nothing but an incompetent Duelist with no spirit.

00:18:04.100 --> 00:18:05.060
What a laugh!

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:10.020
That's my line! You sure you should be so happy about such a small amount of damage?!

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:12.400
This match is just beginning!

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:13.860
What?

00:18:13.860 --> 00:18:16.860
I activate Rai Rider's Monster Effect!

00:18:16.860 --> 00:18:21.580
The Monster who battles with this Monster can't battle during my opponent's next turn!

00:18:21.580 --> 00:18:24.160
Hmph, and that's all your spirit can offer?

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:26.460
Your field's completely empty!

00:18:26.460 --> 00:18:29.040
This ends on my turn!

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:32.790
I set a card face-down and end my turn.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:39.470
Go, Black Mist!

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:47.890
My turn! Draw!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.480
I Summon Blade Bouncer!

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:57.070
I then Direct Attack with Hammer-Rush Bouncer!

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:02.870
If I control no Magic or Trap Cards when this card attacks,

00:19:02.870 --> 00:19:06.580
the opposing player can't activate any of their Magic and Trap Cards!

00:19:06.580 --> 00:19:11.290
In other words, no matter what card you set, you can't use any of them!

00:19:11.290 --> 00:19:14.750
So that's why he hasn't set any cards?!

00:19:14.750 --> 00:19:20.680
This is bad! If this attack goes through, Yuma-<i>kun</i> will be left with only 100 Life Points!

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:23.470
Go, Hammer-Rush Bouncer!

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.510
Destroy Knuckle!!

00:19:33.560 --> 00:19:34.520
Yuma!

00:19:34.520 --> 00:19:36.570
H-He was hit!

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:39.400
A spineless coward with nothing but talk.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:42.360
All I need to do is finish you off with Blade Bouncer.

00:19:46.370 --> 00:19:48.750
What?! 1600 Life?!

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:54.210
His Monster protected him!

00:19:54.210 --> 00:20:00.420
Gagaga Gardna can be Special Summoned from my hand in Attack Mode when I receive a Direct Attack.

00:20:00.420 --> 00:20:04.850
And by discarding a card from my hand, I can negate the battle!

00:20:06.300 --> 00:20:09.180
At the same time Hammer-Rush Bouncer attacked directly,

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:12.600
he Special Summoned Gagaga Gardna to nullify the damage

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:17.190
and discarded a card from his hand to prevent Gagaga Gardna from being destroyed.

00:20:20.690 --> 00:20:24.570
But you still take damage equal to the difference in the Monsters' Attack Points.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.530
Gagaga Gardna has 1500 Attack Points.

00:20:27.530 --> 00:20:31.330
I attack using the 1800 Attack Power Blade Bouncer!

00:20:31.330 --> 00:20:33.870
Go! Straight Slash!!

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:36.040
Stop this!

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:42.670
I discard a card from my hand to activate Gagaga Gardna's Monster Effect!

00:20:47.890 --> 00:20:48.930
Yuma!

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:51.520
He takes another 300 points of damage!

00:20:51.930 --> 00:20:56.650
But now the battle's over and I managed to protect Gagaga Gardna.

00:20:56.650 --> 00:20:58.110
Are you sure about that?

00:20:58.400 --> 00:21:01.610
I activate Blade Bouncer's Monster Effect!

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:08.070
By discarding a card from my hand, this Monster can attack once again!

00:21:08.070 --> 00:21:09.790
Once again?!

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:11.660
He's got four cards in his hand.

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:15.790
Even if he manages to endure this attack, he can still attack four more times?!

00:21:15.790 --> 00:21:19.750
Go, Blade Bouncer! Attack Gagaga Gardna!

00:21:19.750 --> 00:21:21.880
Straight Slash!!

00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:23.920
Gagaga Gardna!

00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:28.090
I discard a card from my hand to activate Gagaga Gardna's Monster Effect!

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:36.190
Yuma!

00:21:36.190 --> 00:21:38.650
Now your hand is at zero.

00:21:38.650 --> 00:21:42.650
Regardless of your spirit, you won't be able to use Gagaga Gardna's effect.

00:21:44.400 --> 00:21:46.320
Just give up.

00:21:46.320 --> 00:21:48.660
I activate Blade Bouncer's Monster Effect!

00:21:51.790 --> 00:21:53.540
Go, Blade Bouncer!

00:21:53.540 --> 00:21:55.330
Attack Gagaga Bouncer!

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:57.620
Straight Slash!!

00:22:02.670 --> 00:22:04.550
Gagaga Gardna!

00:22:19.770 --> 00:22:22.940
<i>Someone gave me some water.</i>

00:22:23.320 --> 00:22:28.860
<i>So I was able to paint a rainbow with ease.</i>

00:22:29.990 --> 00:22:34.790
<i>I want to become someone perfect.</i>

00:22:35.580 --> 00:22:37.830
<i>But it's very difficult.</i>

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:41.420
<i>Even with me suffering,</i>

00:22:41.540 --> 00:22:45.510
<i>I can't seem to grasp victory.</i>

00:22:46.380 --> 00:22:48.300
<i>I want to bloom!</i>

00:22:48.840 --> 00:22:52.760
<i>I must be having some kind of weird dream.</i>

00:22:52.760 --> 00:22:55.810
<i>But If I must fulfill this,</i>

00:22:56.310 --> 00:22:59.100
<i>Then I don't mind being laughed at for it.</i>

00:22:59.270 --> 00:23:06.190
<i>Since it's because your limits are decided on your own.</i>

00:23:06.480 --> 00:23:09.240
<i>I'll show it, overcoming it to tomorrow.</i>

00:23:09.490 --> 00:23:13.700
<i>Ah, I'm aiming for the big blue sky.</i>

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:15.660
<i>For all of its glory.</i>

00:23:15.660 --> 00:23:17.450
<i>The Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:22.830
<i>All of those countless flower petals</i>

00:23:23.040 --> 00:23:25.880
<i>They came at the expense of</i>

00:23:26.710 --> 00:23:29.470
<i>me being able to reach those heights.</i>

00:23:29.840 --> 00:23:33.890
<i>Ah, even though I lost my way today,</i>

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:35.720
<i>I still yearn for it.</i>

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:38.020
<i>That Freesia of Desire.</i>

00:23:41.270 --> 00:23:45.770
I've been cornered in my Duel with Droite and Gauche while Astral's gone missing.

00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:49.610
Please come back!

00:23:49.610 --> 00:23:52.200
Are you off fighting somewhere?!

00:23:52.200 --> 00:23:54.700
I can feel you bringing it to them!

00:23:54.700 --> 00:23:57.450
If I lose this Duel, Astral's gonna disappear!

00:23:57.450 --> 00:23:59.290
I won't let that happen!

00:23:59.290 --> 00:24:01.830
This is our bond!

00:24:01.830 --> 00:24:04.210
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal!

00:24:04.210 --> 00:24:07.210
"Connect the Hope Together! Hope Sword Mars Slash!!"

00:24:07.210 --> 00:24:09.090
I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:24:10.880 --> 00:24:14.010
Yuma, were you aware that mice sometimes crawl around your room late at night?

00:24:14.010 --> 00:24:16.260
Are you serious?! I better call an exterminator!

00:24:16.260 --> 00:24:19.640
What are you talking about? I've gathered up a bunch of talented Duelists.

00:24:19.640 --> 00:24:22.100
I named them "Chuma"!
 (Chuu: The sound mice make)

00:24:22.100 --> 00:24:24.730
Am I supposed to get along with them?!
